#            willing to store; the third finishes what the feature was for.
#
#            2f27b03 intake — both write paths filtered incoming answers to the
#              known *key* set and then stored whatever value arrived with the
#              key. A key set is only half a guard: `{"legal_name": {"$ne":
#              null}}` has a legal key, so the firm console showed the company's
#              legal name as "[object Object]". Worse on a required `select` —
#              `isAnswered` counts any non-blank value and the option check ran
#              inside a `typeof value === 'string'` *condition*, so a non-string
#              skipped the check instead of failing it, and a questionnaire
#              could be submitted with a revenue stage that is neither offered
#              choice. narrowIntakeAnswers now filters keys *and* value shapes,
#              shared by both repos; select / boolean / text each reject a
#              wrong-typed scalar with an error the client can see. Free text
#              also gained a ceiling (300 / 5,000 code points) — the portal
#              write endpoint is anonymous, so the only prior bound was
#              Fastify's 1 MB body cap, per save, forever. This closes the gap
#              this file carried as unresolved last round.
#            cbe2a11 intake UI — the two surfaces render the same schema and had
#              each grown their own answer<->control conversion. They disagreed
#              on one case, and it was not cosmetic: the valuation wizard read
#              the blank option of a yes/no field as `false`, so a client who
#              left "Any pending litigation?" unselected recorded a denial they
#              never made — and `false` counts as answered, so the completion
#              tracker then stopped asking for the real one. One implementation,
#              two callers; empty is always null.
#            b047893 intake — the feature stopped one step short of its purpose.
#              A firm could send the link, watch it fill in and read what came
#              back, then had to retype every answer by hand. The `converted`
#              status existed, was styled and labelled, and no code path could
#              produce it. POST /api/v1/firm/intake-links/:id/convert creates
#              the valuation, copies the answers into the engagement's own
#              questionnaire, seeds the five params that land in a typed column,
#              and claims the link — one transaction, row locked first, because
#              `valuation_id` is the only thing making conversion once-only and
#              a double-click would otherwise own two engagements for one client
#              with the second orphaned.
